  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Steps to reproduce (if affected):\n\n1. Open VRChat\n\n2. VRChat experiences a lag on initial log in. Debug log will report `Warning    -  [Always] API websocket connection attempt failed (timeout=True), retrying in a bit...` every 30 seconds.\n\n3. Debug log reports the following several times a second: `[API] Could not ExecuteIfConnected - api is NULL!`\n\n4. After approximately 8 minutes, VRChat experiences a severe lag that lasts for over a minute and then goes back to normal, but the above debug logs still run.\n\nPossibly helpful notes:\n\nMultiple users reporting this issue on Discord user support:.\n\n- https://discord.com/channels/189511567539306508/1259031429099290696/1259031429099290696\n\n- https://discord.com/channels/189511567539306508/1259334158342295624/1259334158342295624\n\nAnother user I know reported the same issue to me.\n\nA steam thread from 2020 has a similar error which had a temporary fix relating to using wifi instead of ethernet cable. I confirmed with all three affected users are on ethernet cable.\n\n- https://steamcommunity.com/app/438100/discussions/5/2145343824294176440?l=portuguese\n\nThis same error appears to have occurred almost exactly a year ago and was fixed in update 2023.2.3p2\n\n- https://vrchat.canny.io/bug-reports/p/launching-vrchat-from-the-website-leads-to-inability-to-receive-notifications-in\n\n- https://vrchat.canny.io/bug-reports/p/error-spam-in-debug-console-in-offline-mode",
